          "parts": [
            {
              "text": "In Queensland, boutique firms commonly use tailored billing structures to improve access to justice. In **family law**, contingency (\"no-win, no-fee\") agreements are prohibited by law, but firms can legally offer **deferred-fee arrangements** (where payment is delayed until a property or financial settlement is finalized) or partner with legal finance providers like JustFund. For **wills and estates**, fixed fees are standard for drafting, while deferred fees often apply to estate administration (paid once assets are liquidated).\n\nSeveral Brisbane-based boutique law firms provide these options:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Forest Lake Law Practice (Brisbane CBD & Western Suburbs)\n*Practices in Family Law, Wills & Estates, and Property Law.*\n* **Free Initial Consultation:** Offers a free 20-minute initial consultation for prospective clients.\n* **Fixed-Fee Wills:** Fixed-price packages are available for standard wills, Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOAs), and Advanced Health Directives.\n* **Deferred Fees:** Explicitly accepts deferred payment arrangements for family law property settlements, allowing clients whose money is tied up in matrimonial assets to pay when the matter resolves.\n\n### 2. Nurture Law (Brisbane & Moreton Bay)\n*Boutique firm specializing exclusively in Wills, Estates, and Probate.*\n* **Free Initial Consultation:** Offers an obligation-free 15-minute phone consultation to evaluate your matter.\n* **Fixed-Fee Wills & Estate Planning:** Provides transparent fixed pricing for standard and complex estate planning documents.\n* **Deferred Fees (Estate Administration):** If you are an executor or administrator, or a beneficiary waiting on an entitlement, they offer deferred billing where fees are paid only after estate assets are sold or released.\n\n### 3. Bespoke Legal Group (Brisbane & Gold Coast)\n*Boutique firm covering Family Law, Estate Planning, and Conveyancing.*\n* **Free Initial Consultation:** Offers a free 20-minute initial consultation specifically for family law inquiries.\n* **Fixed-Fee Wills:** Clearly published fixed fees for standard wills, as well as discounted dual packages combining a Will and EPOA.\n* **Payment Plans:** Provides formal, interest-free payment plan options to spread the cost of professional fees across manageable intervals.\n\n### 4. Barton Family Lawyers (Brisbane CBD)\n*Dedicated boutique family law firm.*\n* **Deferred Fees (\"Pay at Settlement\"):** Specializes in property division where one partner lacks liquid funds. They offer in-house deferred fee agreements for qualified cases as well as integration with JustFund (a family law litigation funder that pays the fees throughout the case, with repayment deferred until final property settlement).\n* **Staged & Fixed Fees:** Provides staged and fixed pricing for discrete steps (e.g., drafting consent orders, mediation, or court steps) rather than open-ended hourly billing.\n\n### 5. Ramsden Family Law (Brisbane CBD)\n*Boutique family law division.*\n* **Free Initial Case Assessment:** Provides a complimentary intake session to evaluate the legal viability of your case.\n* **Deferred Fees:** Offers a formal \"Pay at the End\" model (partnered with JustFund) allowing clients with limited cash flow but substantial asset equity to access representation with zero upfront legal fees until settlement.\n\n### 6. Kate Redman & Associates (Brisbane)\n*Boutique mobile and virtual firm focusing strictly on Wills and Estates.*\n* **Fixed-Fee Estate Planning:** An all-female boutique that operates entirely on transparent, upfront fixed pricing for wills, testamentary trusts, and EPOAs, with home/hospital visits available across Brisbane.\n* **Free Scoping Call:** Offers short preliminary discussions to assess your estate needs before issuing a fixed quote.\n\n---\n\n### Questions to Ask Before Signing an Agreement\n1. **Deferred Fees:** Does the firm carry the deferred balance on their own ledger, or do they refer you to a third-party litigation funder (such as JustFund)? If third-party, check what interest rate or application fees apply.\n2. **Outlays/Disbursements:** Even with deferred professional fees, courts and government bodies charge out-of-pocket fees (filing fees, title searches, probate advertising). Ask whether you must cover outlays as they occur.\n3. **Fixed-Fee Scope:** For wills, verify what counts as a \"standard\" will versus a \"complex\" will (e.g., blending families, business assets, or testamentary discretionary trusts often carry higher fixed tiers).",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
